            "rationale": "All three resolver mutants (include-resolver hidden, module path flattened, 2018 sibling ignored) make the golden differ.",
            "failure_scenario": "A surviving mutant would mean the fixture cannot tell the 2018-layout rule from its absence.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "merge_attr_mutant_killed",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "cargo check with the attribute restored: non-zero exit (killed); the unmutated head checks clean."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "cargo",
              "check",
              "-p",
              "aprender-contracts",
              "--lib"
            ],
            "exit_code": 101,
            "stdout_sha256": "f422d15c4d17dd7633b5eeadc2275e0daa9a109ab07e13c5a7539919bc8813df",
            "rationale": "Restoring the auto-merged #[path] in json/mod.rs makes the crate fail to build, so dropping it is required, not cosmetic.",
            "failure_scenario": "Had the build passed with the attribute, the line would be harmless and the resolution untested.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
